    "text": "2. Lamkin\u2013Tkocz, arXiv:2001.06439v3, Conjecture 1: every iid nonnegative law and every real p>1 gives log-convex E[(S_n/n)^p]. Actual original statement/Remark 6 and Gon\u00e7alves\u2013Madrid\u2013Ramos arXiv:2608.00813v1 Theorem 1/Corollary 2 and application were read. Their convex-order theorem for products of disjoint normalized blocks applies to partitions (n,n) majorized by (n+1,n-1) of 2n. Testing with t^p and using independence gives exactly b_n^2 <= b_(n-1)b_(n+1), for all n>=2. Already public on 1 August 2026. Classical convex order of linear averages alone does NOT suffice: (uv)^p has Hessian determinant p^2(1-2p)u^(2p-2)v^(2p-2)<0. The new public product theorem supplies precisely the missing bridge. No new result claimed."
